  "title": "Pattie Boyd profile and pictures",
  "date": null,
  "content": "<div class=\"breadcrumbs\" typeof=\"BreadcrumbList\" vocab=\"https://schema.org/\">\n<span property=\"itemListElement\" typeof=\"ListItem\"><a property=\"item\" typeof=\"WebPage\" title=\"Go to Beatle people.\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/\" class=\"post post-page\"><span property=\"name\">Beatle people</span></a><meta property=\"position\" content=\"1\"></span> » <span property=\"itemListElement\" typeof=\"ListItem\"><span property=\"name\" class=\"post post-page current-item\">Pattie Boyd</span><meta property=\"url\" content=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/\"><meta property=\"position\" content=\"2\"></span></div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></span> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/3/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/4/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></a></div><p>Pattie Boyd met <a href=\"/people/george-harrison/\">George Harrison</a> in 1964 on the set of the <em>A Hard Day’s Night</em> film. They married on <a href=\"/1966/01/21/george-harrison-marries-pattie-boyd/\">21 January 1966</a>. <span id=\"more-421\"></span></p><blockquote><div>We got on a train at Marylebone Station one day and the train took off – and suddenly we were in a film! And in the film there were little schoolgirls in gym-slips, who were actually models, and we were quite fascinated with them – George even married one: Pattie Boyd.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>She was born Patricia Anne Boyd on 17 March 1944, in Taunton, Somerset. The eldest of four siblings, Boyd attended convent boarding schools until 1961, and moved to London the following year.</p><p>Boyd began modeling in 1962, but was rejected by many photographers because of her unusual looks. She went on to model in London, New York and Paris, and was photographed by David Bailey and Terence Donovan; Twiggy later said she based her look on Boyd’s.</p><p>Boyd met George Harrison in 1964, when she was 19, after being cast as a schoolgirl fan in <em>A Hard Day’s Night</em>. At the time she was in a relationship with another man, Eric Swayne, and initially declined Harrison’s request for a date.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-421 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1966-photos/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTY2IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE2NiI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"166\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001-200x166.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 1966\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001-200x166.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001.jpg 476w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"12125\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1966-photos/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"476,396\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 1966\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_001.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1966-photos/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTQ2IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE0NiI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"146\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003-200x146.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 1966\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003-200x146.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003-580x423.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003.jpg 730w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"12127\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1966-photos/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"730,532\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 1966\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-harrison-pattie-boyd_003.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><blockquote><div>On first impressions, <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John</a> seemed more cynical and brash than the others, <a href=\"/people/ringo-starr/\">Ringo</a> the most endearing, <a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul</a> was cute and George, with velvet-brown eyes and dark chestnut hair, was the best-looking man I had ever seen. At a break for lunch I found myself sitting next to him. Being close to him was electrifying.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Pattie Boyd<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a></div><p>One of the first things he said to her was “Will you marry me?” When she laughed, Harrison said, “Well, if you won’t marry me, will you have dinner with me tonight?” Several days later, again on the film set, he asked her out once more and she accepted, having by then ended her relationship with Swayne.</p><p>Their first date took place at the Garrick Club, a private gentlemen’s club in Covent Garden, London. Also present was The Beatles’ manager <a href=\"/people/brian-epstein/\">Brian Epstein</a>, as Boyd later recounted in her 2007 autobiography <a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a> (<em>Wonderful Tonight</em> in the USA).</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/1966-photos/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-12130\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSI4MDQiIGhlaWdodD0iNDE4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgODA0IDQxOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"12130\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1966-photos/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"804,418\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison with Brian Epstein, 1966\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001.jpg\" data-src=\"/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001.jpg\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison with Brian Epstein, 1966\" width=\"804\" height=\"418\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-12130\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001.jpg 804w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001-580x302.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001-200x104.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/66_george-pattie-harrison-brian-epstein_001-768x399.jpg 768w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 804px) 100vw, 804px\"></a></p><blockquote><div>I didn’t resent [Brian’s] presence on our first date – he was good company and seemed to know everything about wine, food and restaurants.<p></p><p>And perhaps if George and I, two young, shy people, had been on our own in such a grown-up restaurant, it would have been too intense.</p><p>As it was, we had a lovely evening and sat side by side on a banquette listening to Brian, hardly daring to touch each other’s hand.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Pattie Boyd<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a></div><p>Boyd and Harrison quickly became an item, and in May 1964 they went on holiday to Tahiti for four weeks with John and <a href=\"/people/cynthia-lennon/\">Cynthia Lennon</a>. It was an attempt to escape from the pressures of Beatlemania, and each of them traveled under a false name – Boyd was Miss Bond, the girlfriend of Mr Hargreaves.</p><blockquote><div>Cynthia and Pattie had long black wigs which they wore as disguises. John and I put their wigs on, and our oilskin macs, and made a little 8mm film about natives on an island with a missionary, John, who comes out of the ocean to convert them.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">George Harrison<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-2\" class=\"gallery galleryid-421 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzUiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM1IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"135\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02-135x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison, Bahamas, 1965\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02-135x200.jpg 135w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02-392x580.jpg 392w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02-648x960.jpg 648w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02-768x1137.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02.jpg 982w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 135px) 100vw, 135px\" data-attachment-id=\"25693\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"982,1454\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison, Bahamas, 1965\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/65-george-pattie-harrison-bahamas_02-648x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div cla